The two work well together: Theft Detection Lock puts the thief in front of the lock screen, and CrookCatcher photographs whoever tries to get past it. It also covers the cases Theft Detection Lock ignores, like a phone taken from a table or someone at home guessing your PIN.

CrookCatcher has been downloaded more than 12 million times since 2014 and takes around 1.2 million intruder photos a day. Setup takes a few minutes: see [how to see who tried to unlock your Android phone](/blog/see-who-tried-to-unlock-your-phone).

